        <div id="buyer-feedback" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            8. What Do Buyers Say About Glo Taste and Mixing?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Buyers are split, and the split is mostly about the reformulation. The brand's product page shows an average of 4.64 out of 5 from 935 reviews collected by its own review app. In the 106 most recent reviews we read (late September to mid November 2026), 64 were five-star, 7 four-star, 11 three-star, 11 two-star and 13 one-star, with a few duplicated posts. These are brand-hosted reviews, not an independent sample.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What buyers praise</h3>

          <p>
            Positive reviewers most often mention flavor, with Chocolate singled out as rich and bittersweet, and several say it is the first protein powder that has not upset their stomach or left them bloated. Others say it keeps them full between meals, works well in coffee or Greek yogurt, and has no artificial aftertaste. A few buyers with PCOS say the myo-inositol and the short ingredient list were why they chose it, and one reviewer after bariatric surgery valued that it contains no pea protein.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What buyers complain about</h3>

          <p>
            The most common complaint is from long-time GLO customers who say the new formula does not taste or mix like the old one. Repeated themes are a strong coconut flavor (the coconut milk powder is new), clumping or foam even with a blender, an aftertaste some call chalky or milky, a darker and more bitter chocolate, and "too sweet" from others. One buyer who cannot have coconut said the ingredient change was not flagged when the name changed. A smaller group reports slow replies from customer service on returns, and several mention the price.
          </p>

          <p>
            The practical takeaway: if you never tried GLO, the reviews suggest most new buyers like OURS, particularly Chocolate. If you loved the original GLO, expect a different product and buy one bag before subscribing. Buyers who struggled with clumps report better results with a blender and the 6 to 10 oz of liquid the brand recommends, though not everyone found that fixed it.
          </p>
